<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 2 October, from 1187 to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/saladin" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saladin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1187">1187 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">839 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Saladin takes Jerusalem from the Crusaders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a short siege, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> accepted the surrender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, ending 88 years of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader</a> rule. Most inhabitants were allowed to ransom themselves, and the city's loss prompted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1780">1780 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">246 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Major John André is hanged as a British spy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Major John André, captured carrying Benedict Arnold's plans to surrender West Point, was hanged at Tappan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. His composure won sympathy even among his captors, while Arnold's name became a byword for treason.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1835">1835 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">191 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Texan settlers fire the first shots of the Texas Revolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Gonzales, Texan colonists refused to hand back a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> to Mexican troops and fired on them beneath a flag reading 'Come and Take It'. The skirmish opened the war that led to Texan independence in 1836.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1869">1869 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">157 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mohandas Gandhi is born in Porbandar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mohandas <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karamchand-gandhi">Karamchand Gandhi</a> was born in Porbandar, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s western coast. His method of non-violent mass resistance, satyagraha, drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> movement and inspired civil rights campaigns worldwide.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mexican troops open fire on students at Tlatelolco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soldiers and police fired on a student rally in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plaza-de-las-tres-culturas">Plaza de las Tres Culturas</a>, ten days before the Olympic Games opened. Estimates of the dead range from about 30 to several hundred; the government long concealed the toll.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlatelolco">Tlatelolco</a></div></div></li></ol>
